<h2 class="heading margin-top-md" id="cart">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-shopping-bag">
        <path d="M6 2L3 6v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V6l-3-4z"></path>
        <line x1="3" y1="6" x2="21" y2="6"></line>
        <path d="M16 10a4 4 0 0 1-8 0"></path>
    </svg>
    Cart</h2>
<h3 id="c-all">Get all carts</h3>
<pre><code>fetch(<span class="c-api">'https://fakestoreapi.com/carts'</span>,{
            headers:{"Authorization":"Bearer &lt;your token&gt;"}
        })
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<p>
    <span class="tips">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="feather feather-zap">
            <polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"></polygon>
        </svg>
    </span>Every cart route needs a token. You get back your own carts; an admin gets
    everyone's. If you have no cart at all, an empty one is created for you and returned.
</p>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
            [
                {
                    id:1,
                    userId:1,
                    date:2020-10-10,
                    products:[{productId:2,quantity:4},{productId:1,quantity:10},{productId:5,quantity:2}]
                },
                <span class="c-comment">/*...*/</span>
                {
                    id:20,
                    userId:10,
                    date:2019-10-10,
                    products:[{productId:1,quantity:5},{productId:5,quantity:1}]
                }
            ]
        </code></pre>


<h3 id="c-single">Get a single cart</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts/5'</span>)
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
            {
                id:5,
                userId:1,
                date:...,
                products:[...]
            }
        </code></pre>



<h3 id="c-limit">Limit results</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts?limit=5'</span>)
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
        [
            {
                id:1,
                userId:1,
                date:...,
                products:[...]
            },
            <span class="c-comment">/*...*/</span>
            {
                id:5,
                userId:1,
                date:...,
                products:[...]
            }
        ]
        </code></pre>



<h3 id="c-sort">Sort results</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts?sort=desc'</span>)
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<p>
    <span class="tips">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="feather feather-zap">
            <polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"></polygon>
        </svg>
    </span>The default value is in ascending mode, you can use it with 'desc' or 'asc' as you want.
</p>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
        [
            {
                id:20,
                userId:1,
                date:...,
                products:[...]
            },
            <span class="c-comment">/*...*/</span>
            {
                id:1,
                userId:1,
                date:...,
                products:[...]
            }
        ]
        </code></pre>




<h3 id="c-date">Get carts in a date range</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts/startdate=2019-12-10&enddate=2020-10-10'</span>)
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<p>
    <span class="tips">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="feather feather-zap">
            <polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"></polygon>
        </svg>
    </span>If you don't add any start date it will fetch from the beginning of time and if you don't add any end date it
    will fetch until now.
    You can also use limit(Number) and sort(asc|desc) as a query string to get your ideal results
</p>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
    [
        {
            id:1,
            userId:1,
            date:2019-12-10,
            products:[...]
        },
        <span class="c-comment">/*...*/</span>
        {
            id:4,
            userId:1,
            date:2020-10-10,
            products:[...]
        }
    ]
        </code></pre>






<h3 id="c-user-cart">Get user carts</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts/user/2'</span>)
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<p>
    <span class="tips">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="feather feather-zap">
            <polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"></polygon>
        </svg>
    </span>You can also use date range as query string to get your ideal results
</p>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
            [
            {
                id:5,
                userId:2,
                date:2019-10-03,
                products:[...]
            },
            <span class="c-comment">/*...*/</span>
            {
                id:6,
                userId:2,
                date:2020-10-10,
                products:[...]
            }
        ]
        </code></pre>




<h3 id="c-new">Add a product to your cart</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts'</span>,{
            method:"POST",
            headers:{"Authorization":"Bearer &lt;your token&gt;"},
            body:JSON.stringify(
                {
                    productId:5,
                    quantity:1
                }
            )
        })
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<p>
    <span class="tips">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="feather feather-zap">
            <polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"></polygon>
        </svg>
    </span>The product is added to <em>your</em> cart, resolved from your token - there is no
    cart id in the path, and <span class="c-api">userId</span> is never read from the body.
    <span class="c-api">quantity</span> defaults to 1, and adding a product that is already
    in the cart increases its quantity instead of creating a second line.
    <span class="c-api">priceAtAdd</span> is stamped from the catalog, so anything you send
    for it is ignored. Cart writes are customer-only: an admin token gets a 403.
    remember that the data will really be inserted into the database.
</p>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
            {
                id:21,
                userId:5,
                date:2020-02-03,
                products:[{productId:5,quantity:1,priceAtAdd:109.95}]
            }
        </code></pre>



<h3 id="c-update">Update a product in your cart</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts/products/1'</span>,{
            method:"PUT",
            headers:{"Authorization":"Bearer &lt;your token&gt;"},
            body:JSON.stringify(
                {
                    quantity:3
                }
            )
        })
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts/products/1'</span>,{
                method:"PATCH",
                headers:{"Authorization":"Bearer &lt;your token&gt;"},
                body:JSON.stringify(
                    {
                        quantity:3
                    }
                )
            })
                .then(res=>res.json())
                .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<p>
    <span class="tips">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="feather feather-zap">
            <polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"></polygon>
        </svg>
    </span>The id in the path is a <em>product</em> id, and the cart is your own.
    <span class="c-api">quantity</span> is the only editable field - it must be a whole
    number of at least 1 - and the original <span class="c-api">priceAtAdd</span> snapshot
    is left alone. It returns your whole updated cart.
    remember that the data will really be updated in the database.
</p>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
            {
                id:7,
                userId:3,
                date:2019-12-10,
                products:[{productId:1,quantity:3,priceAtAdd:109.95}]
            }
        </code></pre>



<h3 id="c-delete-product">Delete a product from your cart</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts/products/2'</span>,{
            method:"DELETE",
            headers:{"Authorization":"Bearer &lt;your token&gt;"}
        })
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<p>
    <span class="tips">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="feather feather-zap">
            <polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"></polygon>
        </svg>
    </span>The product with the given id will be removed from your cart. the update will really be saved to the database
    and it will return you the updated cart.
</p>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
            {
                id:6,
                userId:...,
                date:...,
                products:[{productId:1,quantity:5,priceAtAdd:22.3}]
            }
        </code></pre>


<h3 id="c-delete">Delete a cart</h3>
<pre><code>fetch('<span class="c-api">https://fakestoreapi.com/carts/6'</span>,{
            method:"DELETE",
            headers:{"Authorization":"Bearer &lt;your token&gt;"}
        })
            .then(res=>res.json())
            .then(json=>console.log(json))</code></pre>
<p>
    <span class="tips">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="feather feather-zap">
            <polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"></polygon>
        </svg>
    </span>You can only delete a cart you own, and an admin token gets a 403 like every other
    cart write. The cart will really be deleted from the database and it will return you the deleted cart.
</p>
<button class="show-output btn btn-outline">Show output</button>
<pre class="output-result"><code>
            <span class="c-comment">//output</span>
            {
                id:6,
                userId:...,
                date:...,
                products:[...]
            }
        </code></pre>